    {
        "name": "Mastitis",
        "name_ja": "乳腺炎",
        "symptoms": {"mammary_swelling", "mammary_redness", "fever", "appetite_loss", "lethargy"},
        "description": "Mastitis is a bacterial infection of the mammary gland in lactating females, causing systemic illness if untreated.",
        "description_ja": "授乳中のメスの乳腺感染。",
        "urgency": "high",
        "recommended_tests": ["physical_exam", "bacterial_culture", "CBC"],
        "causes": "Caused by: 1) Bacterial infection: Staphylococcus spp. (most common), Streptococcus spp., Escherichia coli; 2) Route of infection: damaged nipple tissue (trauma from pup biting, rough bedding), ascending infection from perineum, hematogenous spread; 3) Risk factors: poor cage hygiene, dirty/damp bedding, inadequate nutrition (especially vitamin A/E deficiency impairs immune function), large litter size (increased pup trauma), concurrent illness/immunosuppression.",
        "causes_ja": "ハムスターの乳腺炎の原因：細菌感染（Staphylococcus最多、Streptococcus、E. coli）。感染経路：乳頭損傷（産仔咬傷、粗い床材）、会陰部からの上行感染、菌血症。リスク因子：不良な飼育環境衛生、汚れた/湿った床材、栄養不足（ビタミンA/E欠乏で免疫障害）、大産仔数（産仔外傷増加）、並存疾患/免疫抑制。",
        "pathophysiology": "Mastitis develops when bacteria colonize the mammary gland epithelium, triggering acute inflammatory response. Bacterial toxins cause tissue damage and recruit neutrophils/macrophages. Inflammation causes: glandular swelling, congestion, edema, abscess formation. Lacteal stasis may occur from pain/swelling, leading to secondary milk cake formation. Systemic absorption of bacterial endotoxins and inflammatory mediators causes fever, anorexia, lethargy. In hamsters, small body size permits rapid sepsis progression; untreated mastitis can lead to mammary abscess, septicemia, and maternal death within 3-7 days. Infected milk may be ingested by nursing pups, causing GI infection/diarrhea.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "乳腺炎は細菌が乳腺上皮にコロニー化し急性炎症反応を引き起こす。細菌毒素で組織損傷→好中球/マクロファージ募集。乳腺腫脹、充血、浮腫、膿瘍形成。乳汁停滞が痛み/腫脹で生じ、二次的milk cake形成。細菌エンドトキシン/炎症メディエーターの全身吸収で発熱、食欲不振、沈鬱。ハムスター小体サイズで敗血症が急速進行；未治療乳腺炎は乳腺膿瘍→敗血症→母体死亡（3-7日）。感染乳が授乳産仔に摂取→GI感染/下痢。",
        "treatment": "Immediate intervention critical: 1) Antibiotics empirically (culture pending): Enrofloxacin 10 mg/kg PO/SC q12h OR trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole (TMS) 30 mg/kg PO q12h × 10-14 days. Once culture results available, switch to sensitivity-directed antibiotic. 2) Supportive care: SC/IP fluids (lactated Ringer's 50 mL/kg/day if dehydrated), pain management essential—meloxicam 0.1-0.3 mg/kg SC q12h × 5-7 days (avoid oral meloxicam as hamsters may not eat). 3) Local management: Warm (not hot) compresses q6-8h to affected glands (10-15 min, promotes blood flow), gentle milking if not too painful (may help drain infected fluid). 4) Nursing management: If pups young (<7 days), consider supplemental bottle-feeding with formula (hamster pups start eating solids around day 7); if older pups, they can be weaned earlier (day 15-18 vs normal 21 days). Infected milk is a concern; monitor pups for diarrhea. 5) Surgery if indicated: Mammary abscess drainage/lancing if abscess identified; rarely, partial mastectomy if gland is necrotic/irreversibly damaged. 6) Monitor for complications: Sepsis (high fever, lethargy, shock), secondary infections. Hospitalization recommended for first 48-72h of treatment if severely ill.",
        "treatment_ja": "ハムスター乳腺炎：迅速介入重要：1) 抗菌薬経験的（培養待機）：エンロフロキサシン10 mg/kg PO/SC q12h または TMS 30 mg/kg PO q12h × 10-14日。培養結果で感受性指向性抗菌薬に変更。2) 支持療法：輸液（乳酸リンガー50 mL/kg/日 脱水時）、鎮痛管理重要—メロキシカム0.1-0.3 mg/kg SC q12h × 5-7日（経口メロキシカムは採食低下）。3) 局所管理：温湿布（熱くない）q6-8h（10-15分、血流促進）、痛みが少ないなら温和な搾乳。4) 授乳管理：産仔<7日齢なら補助ボトル給餌考慮（ハムスター産仔は7日齢で離乳食開始）；>7日齢なら早期離乳（21日→15-18日）可能。感染乳が懸念；産仔下痢監視。5) 外科：乳腺膿瘍排膿/穿刺；稀に部分乳腺摘出（壊死/不可逆損傷）。6) 合併症監視：敗血症（高熱、沈鬱、ショック）、二次感染。重症なら最初48-72時間入院推奨。",
        "prevention": "Prevention includes: 1) Hygienic breeding: clean dry bedding (replace daily), remove soiled nesting material, sanitize cages regularly; 2) Nutritional support during lactation (increased caloric/nutrient demand): provide high-quality diet, extra protein (dog/cat food supplement), vitamin A/E supplementation; 3) Minimize nipple trauma: avoid rough bedding (aspen, cedar avoid as toxic), use soft paper bedding; 4) Litter size management: limit to 8-10 pups maximum (natural separation if possible to reduce pup density); 5) Maternal health: ensure adequate rest between litters (minimum 2-week interval), prevent obesity (increases infection risk), regular monitoring during lactation period. 6) Prompt treatment of any injury/illness in breeding female to prevent immunosuppression.",
        "prevention_ja": "ハムスター乳腺炎予防：1) 衛生的育種：清潔な乾燥床材（毎日交換）、汚れた産巣材除去、ケージ定期消毒。2) 授乳期栄養補給（増加カロリー/栄養要求）：高品質食、追加蛋白（犬/猫食補助）、ビタミンA/E補充。3) 乳頭外傷最小化：粗い床材回避（アスペン、スギは毒性）、軟紙製床材使用。4) 産仔数管理：最大8-10頭（可能なら自然分離で産仔密度軽減）。5) 母体健康：産仔間十分な休止（最小2週間）、肥満防止（感染リスク増）、授乳期間定期監視。6) 育種雌の損傷/疾患の迅速治療（免疫抑制予防）。",
        "prognosis": "Good with early aggressive treatment. With antibiotics started within 24-48h of symptoms, cure rate is 80-90%. Delayed treatment (>3-5 days) or sepsis development: mortality 40-60%. Mammary abscess or septicemia requires surgery and intensive care; mortality higher (50-70%). Surviving females may have permanent mammary damage/scarring, making future lactation problematic. Recommendation: spay females after weaning to prevent recurrence.",
        "prognosis_ja": "ハムスター乳腺炎の予後：早期積極的治療で良好。症状発症24-48時間以内に抗菌薬開始で治癒率80-90%。遅延治療（>3-5日）または敗血症発症：死亡率40-60%。乳腺膿瘍または敗血症は外科と集中治療で死亡率高い（50-70%）。生存メスは永続的乳腺損傷/瘢痕化で今後授乳困難。推奨：離乳後避妊手術で再発防止。",
        "onset_pattern": {"acute", "subacute"},
        "age_predisposition": {"adult", "young", "senior"},
    },
